1.bug_scenario:
When highlighting TypeScript generics like “OutT” in a signature such as
type ParseFunc<OutT, InT> = (val: InT) => OutT;
only the “Out” portion is being picked up by the highlighter in the custom TS mode— the trailing “T” is treated as plain text. The snapshots show that “Out” is marked with the “type” color and “T” remains unstyled, so camel-case type parameters are not highlighted as single identifiers.
